-- title:
--   Galois over-layer carrying the unramified level of degree n
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and work inside a fixed algebraic closure `PadicAlgCl q` of $\mathbb{Q}_q$. Let $L$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}_q \subseteq$ `PadicAlgCl q`, finite over $\mathbb{Q}_q$, and let $G$ be a finite group acting faithfully on $L$ by ring automorphisms, together with a compatible action on $L^\times$: the hypotheses state that $g \cdot \iota(x) = \iota(x)$ for all $g \in G$, $x \in \mathbb{Q}_q$, where $\iota$ is the structure map, and that the unit action agrees with the field action after passing to $L$. Let $K \le L$ be a further intermediate field, finite over $\mathbb{Q}_q$, assumed to be exactly the fixed field: an element of $L$ lies in $K$ if and only if it is fixed by every $g \in G$. Let $n > 0$. The conclusion produces an intermediate field $M \supseteq L$, finite over $\mathbb{Q}_q$, a finite group $H$ acting faithfully on $M$ by ring automorphisms with a compatible action on $M^\times$, normal subgroups $N_L, N_n \trianglelefteq H$, an isomorphism $e : G \cong H/N_L$, an element $\varphi \in H$ and a unit $\pi \in M^\times$, such that: $H$ fixes $\mathbb{Q}_q$ pointwise and the unit action is compatible with the field action; $K$ is the fixed field of $H$ in $M$ and $L$ is the fixed field of $N_L$ in $M$; whenever $h \in H$ has class $e(g)$ in $H/N_L$, the automorphisms $g$ and $h$ agree on $L$; $H/N_n$ has exactly $n$ elements and is generated by the class of $\varphi$; for every $x \in M$ fixed by $N_n$ with $\|x\| \le 1$ one has $\|\varphi \cdot x - x^{\,m}\| < 1$, where $m$ is the cardinality of the residue field of the valuation ring of $K$ obtained by pulling back the valuation ring of `PadicAlgCl q`; and $\pi$ is fixed by all of $H$, lies in $K$, satisfies $\|\pi\| < 1$, and is of maximal norm among $N_n$-fixed elements $y$ of $M$ with $\|y\| < 1$.
--
--   The statement packages the existence of an "unramified over-layer datum": any finite Galois layer $L/K$ with group $G$ can be enlarged to a layer $M/K$ with group $H$ which simultaneously realises $L$ (as $M^{N_L}$, with $G \cong H/N_L$) and an unramified extension of $K$ of degree exactly $n$ (as $M^{N_n}$, with $H/N_n$ cyclic generated by a Frobenius element $\varphi$ and with a uniformiser $\pi$ of $K$). It is the existential hypothesis quantified over in the construction and characterisation of the local fundamental class, and is used by [`ExtCitation.LocalLevel.existsUnique_isLocalFundamentalClass`](thm.html#ExtCitation.LocalLevel.existsUnique_isLocalFundamentalClass) and the accompanying compatibility and cohomology-vanishing results.
